{"schema":"autoform-project-map/v1","parts":{"Algebra/orthogonal-polynomials/catalan-type-polynomials":{"part":{"id":"Algebra/orthogonal-polynomials/catalan-type-polynomials","title":"Catalan-type polynomials","results":11,"status":{"can_prove":5,"fully_proved":6},"parts":0,"api":[],"api_total":0,"imports_total":0,"file":"52.json"},"path":[["region:Algebra & Number Theory","Algebra & Number Theory"],["Algebra","Algebra"],["Algebra/orthogonal-polynomials","Orthogonal polynomials and polynomial sequences"],["Algebra/orthogonal-polynomials/catalan-type-polynomials","Catalan-type polynomials"]],"children":[],"edges":[],"links":{"uses":[],"uses_total":0,"used_by":[],"used_by_total":0},"results":[{"id":"Algebra/orthogonal-polynomials/catalan-type-polynomials/trinomial-neg-pow-series","title":"Negative real power of a trinomial as a power series","status":"fully_proved","caption":"Definition","lean":"MetaMathlibExt.trinomialNegPowSeries","summary":"For real numbers $\\lambda$, $c$, $\\alpha$, $\\beta$ and a natural number $m$, this is the formal power series in $t$ with real coefficients","route":"../roadmap/Algebra/orthogonal-polynomials/catalan-type-polynomials/index.html#trinomial-neg-pow-series"},{"id":"Algebra/orthogonal-polynomials/catalan-type-polynomials/constant-coeff-trinomial-neg-pow-series","title":"Constant term of the trinomial series","status":"fully_proved","caption":"Theorem","lean":"MetaMathlibExt.constantCoeff_trinomialNegPowSeries","summary":"For all real numbers $\\lambda, c, \\alpha, \\beta$ and every natural number $m \\ne 0$, the negative real power of the trinomial $c - \\alpha t + \\beta t^m$ with exponent $\\lambda$ as a power series in $t$, that is, the real power $c^{-\\lambda}$ times the binomial series $(1 + u)^{-\\lambda}$ with $u = (-\\alpha t + \\beta t^m)/c$ substituted (where $u = 0$ when $c = 0$), has constant term $c^{-\\lambda}$.","route":"../roadmap/Algebra/orthogonal-polynomials/catalan-type-polynomials/index.html#constant-coeff-trinomial-neg-pow-series"},{"id":"Algebra/orthogonal-polynomials/catalan-type-polynomials/trinomial-neg-pow-series-neg-one","title":"The trinomial series at exponent one","status":"fully_proved","caption":"Theorem","lean":"MetaMathlibExt.trinomialNegPowSeries_neg_one","summary":"For all real numbers $\\alpha, \\beta$ and every natural number $m \\ne 0$, the formal expansion of $(1 - \\alpha t + \\beta t^m)^{-\\lambda}$ in powers of $t$ at $\\lambda = -1$ is the polynomial $1 - \\alpha t + \\beta t^m$ itself.","route":"../roadmap/Algebra/orthogonal-polynomials/catalan-type-polynomials/index.html#trinomial-neg-pow-series-neg-one"},{"id":"Algebra/orthogonal-polynomials/catalan-type-polynomials/kampe-de-feriet-hermite","title":"Kampé de Fériet polynomials","status":"fully_proved","caption":"Definition","lean":"MetaMathlibExt.kampeDeFerietHermite","summary":"For natural numbers $m, n$ and elements $x, y$ of a commutative $\\mathbb{R}$-algebra, the Kampé de Fériet (two-variable Hermite) polynomial is","route":"../roadmap/Algebra/orthogonal-polynomials/catalan-type-polynomials/index.html#kampe-de-feriet-hermite"},{"id":"Algebra/orthogonal-polynomials/catalan-type-polynomials/kampe-de-feriet-hermite-zero","title":"The zeroth Kampé de Fériet polynomial","status":"fully_proved","caption":"Theorem","lean":"MetaMathlibExt.kampeDeFerietHermite_zero","summary":"For every natural number $m$ and all elements $x, y$ of a commutative $\\mathbb{R}$-algebra, $H^m_0(x, y) = 1$.","route":"../roadmap/Algebra/orthogonal-polynomials/catalan-type-polynomials/index.html#kampe-de-feriet-hermite-zero"},{"id":"Algebra/orthogonal-polynomials/catalan-type-polynomials/kampe-de-feriet-hermite-two-two","title":"The second Kampé de Fériet polynomial","status":"fully_proved","caption":"Theorem","lean":"MetaMathlibExt.kampeDeFerietHermite_two_two","summary":"For all real numbers $x$ and $y$, $H^2_2(x, y) = x^2 + 2y$.","route":"../roadmap/Algebra/orthogonal-polynomials/catalan-type-polynomials/index.html#kampe-de-feriet-hermite-two-two"},{"id":"Algebra/orthogonal-polynomials/catalan-type-polynomials/coeff-hermite-shift-mul-trinomial-neg-po","title":"Hermite-shifted Catalan-type polynomials as convolutions","status":"can_prove","caption":"Theorem","lean":"MetaMathlibExt.coeff_hermiteShift_mul_trinomialNegPowSeries","summary":"Write $H_n(x, y) = H^2_n(x, y)$ for the Kampé de Fériet polynomials. For a natural number $m$ and real numbers $\\lambda, z$, write $(1 - m t + z t^m)^{-\\lambda}$ and $(1 - m z t + t^m)^{-\\lambda}$ for the negative real powers of the trinomials $1 - m t + z t^m$ and $1 - m z t + t^m$ with exponent $\\lambda$ as power series in $t$ (for $m \\ge 1$ these are their expansions in powers of $t$), and let…","route":"../roadmap/Algebra/orthogonal-polynomials/catalan-type-polynomials/index.html#coeff-hermite-shift-mul-trinomial-neg-po"},{"id":"Algebra/orthogonal-polynomials/catalan-type-polynomials/coeff-nieto-hermite-series-mul-trinomial","title":"Nieto–Hermite Catalan-type polynomials as convolutions","status":"can_prove","caption":"Theorem","lean":"MetaMathlibExt.coeff_nietoHermiteSeries_mul_trinomialNegPowSeries","summary":"Let $j, k, m, r$ be natural numbers with $k \\le r$ and let $\\lambda, x, y$ be real numbers. Let $E(t) = e^{2yt - t^2}$ be the exponential series, so that its coefficient of $t^n$ is $H_n(y) / n!$ with $H_n$ the Hermite polynomials, and let $F(t)$ be the power series whose coefficient of $t^n$ is $H_n(y) / n!$ when $n \\ge k$ and $j \\mid n - k$, and $0$ otherwise (for $j \\ge 1$ this is the series…","route":"../roadmap/Algebra/orthogonal-polynomials/catalan-type-polynomials/index.html#coeff-nieto-hermite-series-mul-trinomial"},{"id":"Algebra/orthogonal-polynomials/catalan-type-polynomials/coeff-catalan-type-kernel-decomposition","title":"Splitting the numerator of a unified Catalan-type generating function","status":"can_prove","caption":"Theorem","lean":"MetaMathlibExt.coeff_catalanTypeKernel_decomposition","summary":"Let $j, 